<title>NEW ZEALAND: Thin NZ debt market closes with yields unchanged.</title>
<headline>Thin NZ debt market closes with yields unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------Snapshot at close -------------------</p>
<p>Figures in brackets compare against previous day's close</p>
<p>FUTURES					  PHYSICAL YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS (MAR) 92.68  (nil)	  90-DAYS 7.87   (-0.01)</p>
<p>3-YR BONDS   (MAR) 93.00 (PREV 92.99)  02/00   7.03     (nil)</p>
<p>10-YR BONDS  (MAR) 92.77 (PREV 92.70)  11/06   7.25   (-0.03)</p>
<p>OVERNIGHT CASH 7.95 PCT (PREV 7.95)    US 5-YR  6.13 (PREV 6.15)</p>
<p>NZD/USD 0.7072/79 (PREV 0.7072/79)     US 10-YR 6.33 (PREV 6.36)</p>
<p>TWI 67.28 (PREV 67.40)		     US 30-YR 6.58 (PREV 6.60)</p>
<p>--------------------------(Dec 24)------------------------------</p>
<p>* Yields end little changed</p>
<p>* Volumes minimal</p>
<p>* No change expected</p>
<p>New Zealand yields ended little changed on Tuesday after opening slightly lower in line with a firm U.S. Treasuries market.</p>
<p>Dealers said there was virtually no trading in a market already square for the holiday.</p>
